						"Text":
						{
							"$text": "**Available Commands:**\r\n\r\n1. help / ? - Display available commands and their descriptions.\r\n2. dir / ls - Display all of the files and folders in the current directory.\r\n3. pop / .. - Switch back to previous directory (e.g. go back).\r\n4. login - Enter new login credentials to change the user & permissions.\r\n5. cd <directory> - Change directory to navigate within the terminal system.\r\n6. run <file_id> - Execute the exe file.\r\n7. download <file_id> - Download content from target file.\r\n8. scan <file_id> - Scan content from file.\r\n9. read <file_id> - Reading content of file.\r\n10. shutdown / exit - Shutdown the terminal.\r\n\r\n**Additional help**\r\n\r\n> To find a file, try changing directories via cd <directory> and use the dir command to display all available files at the current level\r\n> Some directories require special access. Use the login command to get Admin access. You may have to take a look at the users file to find the credentials.",
							"$ns": "[4442EDC16ABAC1CFA5A5B695986A3659]",
							"$key": "5B6D84D14DD2AA9F0E2605ADC4A36D62"
						}
					}
				],
